    "commit_body": "Replaces the single current-week weekly adjustment with a point-in-time blend of\ntwo honest weekly states, weighted by trading-bars-elapsed this week\n(t = bars/5, Mon~0.2 -> Fri=1.0):\n  comp_adj = calculate_weekly_adjustment(last-completed W-1, two-weeks-ago W-2)\n             (state 1 = what live trader update already used; honest, ~1wk stale)\n  pit_adj  = calculate_weekly_adjustment(partial current week W [reconstructed\n             from daily bars Mon->date, NO future], last-completed W-1)\n             (state 2 = freshest point-in-time, no future bars)\n  w_adj    = (1-t)*comp_adj + t*pit_adj\n\nWhy: the batch/recalc path keyed the weekly on the CURRENT week and read the\nstored COMPLETE Mon-Fri WeeklyScore for a mid-week historical signal = LOOK-AHEAD,\nwhich inflated the backtest (live trader update was always honest via the\nlast-completed-week property). New production helper database/utils/weekly_pit.py\nreconstructs the partial current week point-in-time (validated bit-identical to\nlive score_intraday_logs, mean|delta|=0.28, 97.5% within +/-2).\n\nValidated (ScoreSimulator, no DB writes): look-ahead REMOVED -- 75+ cohort\noptTP15 Mon-vs-Fri gap +8.4pp (state-3 look-ahead) -> -0.0pp (blend); honest 75+\noptTP15 = 53.3% (Wilson-LB 49.6%, clears 45% call BE) vs the inflated 63.6%;\nfakeout SMOOTHED -- Monday-boundary mean |delta overall| 5.99 -> 3.47 (-42%).\n75+ supply -38.6% (the removed entries were look-ahead false positives).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
    "commit_short": "8b59206c3",
